  "body": "## What changed\n\nIssue #3995: a person who reads a stale discovery file knows the token and can compute every token proof. A false server on the freed port of a crashed window could then receive the tool calls of `camcraft-cli --ui`.\n\nThis PR adds one rule for the whole class: the CLI uses a link file only while its window is proved alive.\n\n- **The window holds a lock.** Each window takes an exclusive OS file lock on `<pid>.lock` in the link folder before it writes its link file. It holds the lock for its whole life. The OS releases the lock when the process ends, a crash included. A reused pid cannot hold the lock of an ended process. The window removes the lock file with its link file when it closes.\n- **The CLI tests the lock two times.** It tests the lock before it dials an entry, and again after the hello. The second test closes the gap where the window ends during the exchange.\n  - The lock is held: the entry is used.\n  - The lock is free: the entry is stale. The CLI removes `<pid>.json`, `<pid>.sock` and `<pid>.lock`, logs a warning and never dials the address. It removes only these fixed names in the link folder, never a path read from the file.\n  - No lock can be tested (no lock file, an error): the entry is unproved. The CLI logs why, keeps the file and never dials it.\n  - When no window is left, the CLI exits 3. The message names each skipped entry and its reason. There is no silent fall-back to an unproved window.\n- **std only.** The lock is `std::fs::File::try_lock` (`flock` on Unix, `LockFileEx` on Windows; stable since Rust 1.89, MSRV 1.90). No new dependency, and the same source on Windows, Linux and macOS. This avoids the `libc` / `windows-sys` declarations that held PR #3971.\n- New module `crates/app/src/mcp/link_owner.rs` (the lock and the test). `link.rs` takes the lock in `open`; `link_client.rs` tests it in `connect`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3995-ui-link-owner-lock.md`.\n\n## What stays open (Refs, not Fixes)\n\nThe lock proves that the window runs. It does not prove which socket on a TCP port answers. On Windows, a local process can share the loopback port of a running window (`SO_REUSEADDR`). The fix for that is the named-pipe transport with a check of the server process id. It needs a direct `windows-sys` dependency and a transport decision by the maintainer. It is filed as #4016 (P3, effort:max). On Unix the socket is in a 0700 folder, so this case does not occur there.\n\nThus this PR uses `Refs #3995`. The maintainer can close #3995 when he accepts that #4016 holds the rest.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nA window of an older build writes no lock file. A CLI of this build does not dial it: it exits 3 and says that nothing proves that the window runs. This is on purpose (see the decision record).\n\n## Tests (final head)\n\nPinning tests (new submodule `crates/app/tests/mcp_live/ui_link_owner.rs`, in the existing `mcp_live` suite):\n\n- `ui_link_owner::a_crashed_windows_file_is_removed_and_its_port_is_never_dialed`: a false server holds the port of a crashed window. It gets no connection. The link file and the lock file are removed. Exit 3 with \"is stale\".\n- `ui_link_owner::a_false_server_that_proves_the_token_gets_no_tool_call_when_the_window_has_ended`: the false server reads the token and sends the correct server proof. The window ends during the hello. No tool call reaches the false server.\n- `ui_link_owner::a_link_file_with_no_owner_proof_is_never_dialed`: a file with no lock file is never dialed and is kept. The CLI exits 3 and says why.\n\nChanged tests in `ui_link.rs`: the forged-token test and the proofless false-server test now hold the lock, so that they still reach the token check. The wrong-token test also asserts that the window holds its lock and that the lock file goes when the window closes.\n\nResults:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`): 167 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 29.0 min. The plan is wide because the new `pub mod` line in `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs` maps to all 165 `app::mcp` suites. `mcp_live`: 25 passed. app lib: 311 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base origin/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 19.6 min (the motion twins and `pocket_pass_start`; the diff does not touch them).\n- Example catalog suites: not run apart from the quick plan (which includes `example_catalog`); no post or toolpath changed.\n- No heavy step: this is a P3 PR.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and macOS were not built or run. The lock is std code with no `cfg`, but `LockFileEx` behaviour was not observed on a host here.\n- A second local user was not emulated.\n- A file system where std file locks are not supported (`Unsupported`) was not tested. There the entry is unproved and skipped, by the code path of the no-lock-file test.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-cli --ui` uses a window's link file only while that window holds its lock. A stale file of a crashed window is removed and never dialed, and a link file without that proof is skipped with the reason.\n\nEffort: high (not escalated).\n\nFixes #3995\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
